# CQ 13: Which learning type does a machine learning algorithm use?
#
# 3.3.9, 3.3.11, 3.3.12 and 3.3.17 define the four kinds. The relation is
# functional: an algorithm performs one kind of learning, and a case needing
# both labelled and unlabelled data states semi-supervised learning, 3.3.11,
# rather than two kinds at once. Negative model 03 tests that.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?algorithm ?learningType
WHERE { ?algorithm iso:basedOnLearning ?learningType }
ORDER BY ?algorithm
